    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "525c1df5_26f86fea",
        "filename": "common/ocpc.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 217,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125984
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-10T17:10:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It seemed that we were compensating *twice* in that case. We\u0027d calculate our VSYS target (compensating for the losses), put in the resistances in the charger IC, and it would also compensate VSYS for losses on top of the VSYS value that wrote in. I believe this was leading to excessive current.",
      "parentUuid": "2cacd97e_67b1d29c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 217,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 217,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "ee587f547a8d9c5faddb3638aed7e4ce5370cac4",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "104a856e_1b499d03",
        "filename": "common/ocpc.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 217,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-13T17:03:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This feels tied to the RAA\u0027s specific compensation path though, right?  Because it\u0027ll disable compensation when Rp1 is 0 (so in the beginning for us), but then enable when we have something to set for Rp1.  Do we anticipate this being the same for SM?",
      "parentUuid": "525c1df5_26f86fea",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 217,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 217,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "ee587f547a8d9c5faddb3638aed7e4ce5370cac4",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2e110fcc_cdfede9d",
        "filename": "common/ocpc.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 217,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125984
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-15T23:47:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the double compensation would still occur. In the SM case, it will occur immediately, so perhaps the default check here is insufficient and should be removed entirely.",
      "parentUuid": "104a856e_1b499d03",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 217,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 217,
        "endChar": 22
      },
